+            "content": "# Project documentation discovery\n\nIdentify independently maintained projects from positive ownership and build or\ndeployment evidence. A project can require documentation when its directory has\nno README. A familiar filename by itself does not establish membership.\n\nFor every candidate, explain inclusion or exclusion. Treat test fixtures,\ngenerated output, archived copies, and directories that only group teams or\nprojects as candidates requiring evidence, not maintained projects by default.\nLeave uncertain maintenance or ownership as an unresolved question.\n\nFor each included project, plan individual files for its project README, every\nexisting documentation source that will move, each destination and introduced\ndocumentation index, and every file whose links need repair. Do not include\n`docs/catalog.json`; the source owns that exact file. An explained empty list is\nvalid when evidence shows that no maintained project is present.\n"
